  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1505",
      "html": "<p>Pseudeutropius moolenburghae Weber &amp; de Beaufort, 1913. Family Horabagridae. Size: 100 mm (3.9\") SL. IUCN Red List: Least Concern (last assessed 2018). Etymology: Greek, pseudes = false + Greek, eu = well + keel, in reference to the compressed body of the fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1505",
      "html": "<p>Asia: Sumatra and western Borneo. Type locality: Djambi, Batang Hari River, Sumatra, Indonesia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/pseudeutropius-moolenburghae-2/",
      "html": "<p>Their home are the river systems Batang Hari on Sumatra and Kapuas on Borneo, from where many popular aquarium fish come.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/pseudeutropius-moolenburghae-2/",
      "html": "<p>Soft, acidic water corresponds to natural conditions, but is not necessary for long-term maintenance. The water temperature should be 24-28°C.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/pseudeutropius-moolenburghae-2/",
      "html": "<p>A dimly furnished tank with Cryptocoryne bushes, floating ferns on the surface and dead leaves on the bottom is ideal.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/pseudeutropius-moolenburghae-2/",
      "html": "<p>Pseudeutropius moolenburghae eat all common ornamental fish food, they are not interested in plants.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/pseudeutropius-moolenburghae-2/",
      "html": "<p>As company are suitable e.g. mouth-breeding fighting fish, Rasbora species, coolie loaches etc. Under no circumstances should these delicate catfish be kept along with bullies such as tiger barbs.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1505",
      "html": "<p>Breeding: unreported.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/pseudeutropius-moolenburghae-2/",
      "html": "<p>In the aquarium, these blackwater fish should be acclimated carefully, because from the wild they know practically no bacterial water pollution.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1505",
      "html": "<p>Fishes Indo-Australian Archipelago v. 2, pp 249, Fig. 100.</p>"
    }
  ],
